241
00:12:38,884 --> 00:12:42,053
It's better to make friends with it,
welcome it into your heart.

242
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:46,224
It's only gonna get worse as you age,
so… [grunts]

243
00:12:47,726 --> 00:12:51,146
-Um…
-Where are you going?

244
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:53,690
I think I know something
that might make you feel better.

245
00:12:54,483 --> 00:12:57,486
[dramatic opera music playing]

246
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:20,800
-Honestly, worth it.
-Oh, absolutely.

247
00:13:22,177 --> 00:13:24,763
So, what do we do now?

248
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:30,977
Oona is trying her best.

249
00:13:31,770 --> 00:13:34,856
I know she acts all, like,
cool and awesome, together,

250
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,608
but it's hard on her too.

251
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:40,278
Her mom left her to take care
of her 12-year-old sister.

252
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:42,656
It's not, like,
the coolest move ever, you know?

253
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:44,241
Well, it's not permanent.

254
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:48,495
Yeah. Yeah, I know, but still…

255
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:57,170
Ever get hangry?

256
00:13:57,963 --> 00:14:01,341
You mean, like, when you're so hungry
you get angry?

257
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:03,760
Yeah. Yeah, exactly.

258
00:14:04,678 --> 00:14:05,804
Yeah, I guess.

259
00:14:05,887 --> 00:14:08,056
Well, isn't every emotion
kinda like hanger?

260
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:10,809
Like, you have to ask yourself,

261
00:14:11,935 --> 00:14:14,813
"Am I actually angry right now,
or am I just hungry?"

262
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:17,774
And most of the time,
you eat a granola bar, and you're fine.

263
00:14:18,817 --> 00:14:21,570
Maybe when you're mad,
you can ask yourself, like,

264
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:25,615
"Am I actually mad right now,
or am I maybe a little sad?"

265
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,663
I feel like I'm going through
the same as you right now.

266
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:32,914
Just in reverse.

267
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:35,667
What do you mean?

268
00:14:36,293 --> 00:14:39,337
I just found out some super dark shit
about my mom, and it's…

269
00:14:41,298 --> 00:14:42,716
It's really sad, but it's…

270
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,552
I don't know. I mostly just feel mad,

271
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:49,556
'cause it's so fucking unfair.

272
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:51,933
Unfair that she died?

273
00:14:53,351 --> 00:14:54,352
Yeah.

274
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,354
Yeah.

275
00:14:56,438 --> 00:14:58,565
And now you're realizing that…

276
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:01,526
you're actually just really sad
that you don't have a mum?

277
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:06,239
[Ramona] Yeah.

278
00:15:12,329 --> 00:15:13,496
Do you think she just…

279
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:16,875
doesn't want to be my mum?

280
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:18,710
What?

281
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:21,212
Dude. Maple, no.

282
00:15:23,089 --> 00:15:24,674
No, not at all.

283
00:15:24,758 --> 00:15:27,677
It's just, adults are weird,

284
00:15:27,761 --> 00:15:31,222
and they have, like,
a lot of complex bullshit going on.

285
00:15:33,683 --> 00:15:34,684
I miss her.

286
00:15:36,603 --> 00:15:37,437
[Ramona] Yeah.

287
00:15:42,025 --> 00:15:45,362
Are you gonna stay mad
but secretly sad at Oona forever?

288
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:50,075
Mmm. Undecided.

289
00:15:51,701 --> 00:15:52,535
Are you?

290
00:15:54,245 --> 00:15:55,580
Undecided.

291
00:15:56,247 --> 00:15:57,999
[both chuckle]

292
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:02,087
Think it is very dangerous
that we canoe in the rain?

293
00:16:02,671 --> 00:16:05,090
[Ellis] No, absolutely not.

294
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:13,014
[exhaling]

295
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:16,518
Hey. Bald eagle.

296
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:18,853
Oh, my God.

297
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:24,651
That's so cool.

298
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:29,364
It's so beautiful.

299
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:33,076
Didn't know our bird
was allowed in Canada.

300
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:34,619
[both chuckle]

301
00:16:46,881 --> 00:16:47,882
Um…

302
00:16:49,551 --> 00:16:53,054
There's something
I should probably talk to you about.

303
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:56,891
Sorry to just, like, drop this on you.

304
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:58,852
What?

305
00:17:00,812 --> 00:17:03,106
The other day, after the fair,
when you guys left,

306
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:04,983
your dad told me something kinda intense.

307
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,444
What?

308
00:17:09,404 --> 00:17:11,239
He said he was
with my mom at the hospital…

309
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:13,616
the night that she died.

310
00:17:16,619 --> 00:17:17,996
What the fuck?

311
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:20,248
Yeah. Yeah.

312
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:25,628
Maybe she asked him to take her there.

313
00:17:25,712 --> 00:17:28,256
I mean, they lived close.

314
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:31,050
Yeah, but he said
that they hadn't seen each other

315
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:32,552
since they were teenagers.

316
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:34,471
So I'm just like…

317
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,933
why would he lie about that?

318
00:17:40,685 --> 00:17:43,897
I found, like, paperwork
in my dad's office today.

319
00:17:45,899 --> 00:17:48,985
Gordon made my dad Ramona's guardian
before he died.

320
00:17:50,111 --> 00:17:51,613
So is it kinda sounding like…

321
00:17:52,947 --> 00:17:56,534
your dad might also be Ramona's dad?

322
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:01,790
This is gonna destroy my mom.

323
00:18:02,373 --> 00:18:05,043
-Ellis, I'm so sorry.
-No, don't. It's not your fault.

324
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:08,838
-You shouldn't have to find out like this.
-It's not your fault. It's fine.

325
00:18:10,131 --> 00:18:11,341
Where's that tape?

326
00:18:23,269 --> 00:18:24,270
-Hey.
-Hey.

327
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:26,064
Maple's inside.

328
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:28,483
-Okay.
-We broke a ton of shit.

329
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:30,902
-Really?
-It felt really good. Yeah.

330
00:18:31,653 --> 00:18:33,488
-We both feel better now.
-Nice. Thank you.

331
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:34,405
-Um…
-Yeah.

332
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:36,574
-All good.
-Yeah.

333
00:18:37,909 --> 00:18:40,495
Yeah, no, she, like…
I don't know what she told you, but…

334
00:18:41,329 --> 00:18:44,707
she started talking about my mum. Um…

335
00:18:47,085 --> 00:18:48,962
And then I tried to talk to her about it,

336
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:51,172
and she started freaking out,
which is fair, but…

337
00:18:51,256 --> 00:18:52,173
Right.

338
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:56,010
I don't know. I just made it worse.

339
00:18:56,094 --> 00:18:57,720
-No.
-Yeah.

340
00:18:57,804 --> 00:18:59,222
-But thank you for…
-No.

341
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:01,766
Yeah. Yeah, all good.

342
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:02,851
[Oona] Thanks.

343
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:15,780
What if I'm, like, not enough?

344
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:20,702
For who?

345
00:19:22,996 --> 00:19:23,913
Um…

346
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:27,792
You are.

347
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:50,315
Yeah, I think I'm just gonna
let you guys do your thing.

348
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:52,066
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah.

349
00:19:53,568 --> 00:19:54,402
Okay.

350
00:20:12,003 --> 00:20:13,171
[exhales]

351
00:20:31,022 --> 00:20:32,357
[Goldie] Joe, hi.

352
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:35,944
Can you believe I found this?
I hope you still like mixtapes.

353
00:20:36,903 --> 00:20:39,656
Are mixtapes even a thing anymore?
[laughs softly]

354
00:20:40,198 --> 00:20:41,324
Anyway, I guess the fact

355
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:45,244
my dad never gets rid of anything
is sometimes worthwhile.

356
00:20:46,329 --> 00:20:50,458
I wanted to record something right now
because the baby just kicked.

357
00:20:50,959 --> 00:20:52,293
She could be here any day now.

358
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:54,754
I wonder who she'll be.

359
00:20:55,797 --> 00:20:59,258
I can't wait to meet her,
for us all to be a family.

360
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,902
I hate movies
where they sing-talk the whole time.

361
00:21:17,986 --> 00:21:20,279
-This is insufferable.
-Well, it won Best Picture.

362
00:21:20,363 --> 00:21:23,491
Yeah. Maple, I feel like
when a movie's won Best Picture,

363
00:21:23,574 --> 00:21:25,201
I'm just gonna automatically hate it.

364
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:27,996
What does winning Best Picture even mean?

365
00:21:28,496 --> 00:21:29,664
You like Parasite.

366
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,333
True. True that, yes.

367
00:21:33,084 --> 00:21:34,752
[chuckles] Yeah, okay.

368
00:21:34,836 --> 00:21:36,004
I'll give it a shot.

369
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:47,724
-I'm really gonna miss you this week.
-I'm gonna miss you too.

370
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:54,063
Can Ramona come with us to camp drop-off?

371
00:21:55,398 --> 00:21:56,232
Yeah.

372
00:21:57,859 --> 00:21:58,860
Yeah, sure.

373
00:21:59,819 --> 00:22:00,862
Mmm-hmm.

374
00:22:03,489 --> 00:22:05,366
Whoa, damn. Who's the one in the fishnets?

375
00:22:05,450 --> 00:22:07,744
-See? I told you you'd like it.
-Wow.

376
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:09,454
-Whoa!
-This is the best part.

377
00:22:09,537 --> 00:22:11,622
Don't know if we should be watching this.

378
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:25,386
Happy birthday.

379
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:29,307
Uh, Ramona, I'm sorry about Mom.
I hope you're feeling okay.

380
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:32,101
I'm sorry that you found out that way.
I wanted it--

381
00:22:32,185 --> 00:22:34,062
Just accept the "happy birthday" first.

382
00:22:35,646 --> 00:22:36,647
Thank you.

383
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:39,442
I get it, why you told me.

384
00:22:41,402 --> 00:22:43,654
Just please, please, please,
no more secrets.

385
00:22:43,738 --> 00:22:45,948
Like, no more digging around for stuff.

386
00:22:46,449 --> 00:22:48,993
I think I'm good on the bomb drops
for the rest of my life.

387
00:22:49,077 --> 00:22:50,870
[chuckles] Yeah. Fair enough.

388
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:51,996
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

389
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:57,335
-See you all on the flip.
-See you on the flip.

390
00:23:01,714 --> 00:23:03,299
["Man I Need" playing]

391
00:23:09,806 --> 00:23:10,973
Thank you.

392
00:23:13,059 --> 00:23:14,018
Hi. Hi.

393
00:23:14,811 --> 00:23:17,271
Hi. This is my party. Hi.

394
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:19,232
Hi.

395
00:23:20,441 --> 00:23:22,610
-Hey, man. Sully…
-[Sully] Yes.

396
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,070
…you fucking killed it.

397
00:23:24,153 --> 00:23:26,280
-I love you. You're perfect.
-Thank you so much.

398
00:23:26,364 --> 00:23:29,534
-I don't know what I'd do without you.
-It was a fun challenge, really.

399
00:23:29,617 --> 00:23:30,910
I locked in on this one.

400
00:23:34,372 --> 00:23:35,748
I don't know anyone here.

401
00:23:40,378 --> 00:23:41,212
Yep.

402
00:23:46,134 --> 00:23:48,136
[people chattering indistinctly]

403
00:23:50,054 --> 00:23:50,888
[Ellis] Hey.

404
00:23:53,099 --> 00:23:54,100
Hey.

405
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:56,686
Is Ramona coming?

406
00:23:57,270 --> 00:23:59,605
No. No, she said
she didn't wanna come tonight.

407
00:23:59,689 --> 00:24:01,274
-Oh. Shit. Great.
-Yeah.

408
00:24:04,569 --> 00:24:05,862
[chuckles]

409
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:08,197
'Cause I was thinking all day
about ways to tell her

410
00:24:08,281 --> 00:24:10,575
that she's actually my sister, so…

411
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:13,619
Yeah.

412
00:24:15,371 --> 00:24:16,998
How… How do you know for sure?

413
00:24:17,081 --> 00:24:20,376
I listened to the whole tape. Both sides.

414
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:23,296
Why did I not think
to listen to both sides?

415
00:24:23,379 --> 00:24:24,881
-Oh, yeah, no.
-It's really stupid.

416
00:24:24,964 --> 00:24:26,549
No. You're fine.

417
00:24:26,632 --> 00:24:30,678
Yeah, the whole other side was
from when she was pregnant, so…

418
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:33,639
Oh, my God, Ellis.

419
00:24:33,723 --> 00:24:34,557
[Ellis] Yeah.

420
00:24:35,641 --> 00:24:38,769
-Are you okay?
-Yeah, I think the weirdest part was just…

421
00:24:40,146 --> 00:24:41,647
hearing how in love they were.

422
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:48,446
Sorry, I'm totally ruining your birthday.

423
00:24:48,529 --> 00:24:51,240
No, you're not. No. No, no, not at all.
Not at all. I…

424
00:24:51,324 --> 00:24:53,284
-Little bit.
-I promise you are not.

425
00:24:53,367 --> 00:24:55,828
It's actually the opposite. It…

426
00:24:57,288 --> 00:25:00,041
I, uh, got you something.

427
00:25:01,959 --> 00:25:03,294
-You…
-It's--

428
00:25:03,377 --> 00:25:05,796
-You did not have to do that.
-Yeah, it's whatever.

429
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:07,215
-Thank you.
-Open it.

430
00:25:10,051 --> 00:25:11,802
I can't believe that you did this.

431
00:25:14,931 --> 00:25:16,515
It's really not that much.

432
00:25:17,725 --> 00:25:18,726
You know.

433
00:25:21,395 --> 00:25:24,774
Yeah, not the Mona Lisa, but, you know.

434
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:28,486
This is pretty close to the Mona Lisa.
[chuckles]

435
00:25:28,569 --> 00:25:30,905
-It's really not that much.
-Thank you. No, no.

436
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:33,115
-Thank you so much. I love it. Thank--
-Annie.

437
00:25:33,199 --> 00:25:34,033
Yeah.

438
00:25:34,116 --> 00:25:35,534
-[Rory] Hey.
-Hey. Hi.

439
00:25:36,118 --> 00:25:37,245
Happy birthday.

440
00:25:37,912 --> 00:25:39,121
Thank you so much.

441
00:25:39,622 --> 00:25:42,166
-Hey, man. What's up?
-[Ellis] Yo.

442
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:47,004
-Uh, did you just get here?
-I just got here, yeah.

443
00:25:47,088 --> 00:25:48,547
-Okay. Damn.
-Same.

444
00:25:48,631 --> 00:25:50,967
Your set starts, like…
We'd have to leave pretty soon.

445
00:25:51,592 --> 00:25:52,426
[Annie] Yeah.

446
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:56,472
Rory actually got us tickets
to this, like, club thing?

447
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:59,267
-Yeah, yeah.
-I don't know. To escape Connor's party.

448
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:01,727
-Yeah, no, totally. That's… That's…
-[Rory] Yeah.

449
00:26:01,811 --> 00:26:03,437
I didn't know you were gonna be here.

450
00:26:03,521 --> 00:26:05,231
[Ellis] It's totally fine. That's cool.

451
00:26:05,314 --> 00:26:07,984
-AJ, I'll wait for you outside.
-Cool. I'll see you outside.

452
00:26:08,067 --> 00:26:09,610
-Okay. Good seeing you.
-Yeah. Same.

453
00:26:13,739 --> 00:26:15,658
This… Did you make this frame?

454
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,118
Yeah. It's…

455
00:26:17,201 --> 00:26:19,161
-[laughs] It's ridiculous.
-I know.

456
00:26:20,204 --> 00:26:23,582
-Thank you.
-Yeah. You're welcome. Happy birthday.

457
00:26:24,375 --> 00:26:25,376
Thanks.

458
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:33,759
-Have fun. Sorry. Can't stay. Okay.
-Yeah, I will.

459
00:26:34,969 --> 00:26:36,554
-Yep.
-I'll see you later.

460
00:26:37,054 --> 00:26:38,431
-Yep. You have fun.
-Okay.

461
00:26:39,682 --> 00:26:41,434
-Thank you. Bye.
-Okay.

462
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:02,371
This is so cool. You'll have
the best time. I'm jealous.

463
00:27:02,455 --> 00:27:05,958
-I'll write you letters every single day.
-Bye. I'm here for a week.

464
00:27:06,042 --> 00:27:07,710
Yeah, but write me back, please, okay?

465
00:27:07,793 --> 00:27:09,086
-Okay, bye.
-I love you.

466
00:27:09,170 --> 00:27:11,172
Dude, Maple, you gotta sing hard, okay?

467
00:27:11,255 --> 00:27:14,258
-Bye! Bye!
-Love you! Bye! Bye.

468
00:27:41,077 --> 00:27:42,370
Okay, bitch.

469
00:27:42,453 --> 00:27:44,330
[grunting] Uh, uh, uh, uh.

470
00:27:44,413 --> 00:27:47,666
-You gonna blow this bitch out or what?
-Wait. We have to wait for Annie.

471
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:51,253
-That's her name. She's gonna love it.
-I think she left with Rory already.

472
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:57,218
-But she might come back later.
-Whatever. It's her loss.

473
00:27:57,301 --> 00:27:59,553
She's not gonna get a treat bag,
that's for sure.

474
00:27:59,637 --> 00:28:02,014
And they have Sillybandz in them
and Poot stickers.

475
00:28:02,098 --> 00:28:04,141
And Poot stickers?
Wow, I was a little like… "Mmm."

476
00:28:04,225 --> 00:28:06,227
But now I'm like,
"You know what? Great idea."

477
00:28:06,310 --> 00:28:08,104
And it is her bad. Missing out.

478
00:28:08,729 --> 00:28:10,856
-I think I need a few frosés.
-[gasps]

479
00:28:10,940 --> 00:28:15,236
-Can I join? Come. Immediately, right now.
-Abso-fucking-lutely! Okay, okay, okay.

480
00:28:18,739 --> 00:28:20,991
-Shit. It's amazing.
-Oh, my God.

481
00:28:21,075 --> 00:28:23,077
-What do you want to drink?
-So many people.

482
00:28:24,161 --> 00:28:28,290
Um, I'll do, like, whatever whiskey
they have, on ice. Sorry.

483
00:28:28,374 --> 00:28:30,334
"Whatever whiskey they have, on ice"?

484
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:33,003
-That… Seriously?
-Is that a bad order?

485
00:28:33,087 --> 00:28:34,964
No, it's the coolest order
I've ever heard.

486
00:28:35,047 --> 00:28:38,050
-[girl] Wait, Annie? Annie!
-Two whatever whiskeys they have, on ice.

487
00:28:39,093 --> 00:28:41,595
-Whoa. Yo!
-My guy.

488
00:28:41,679 --> 00:28:44,306
-No way!
-Oh, my God!

